## Table 8 — Codebook of qualitative findings from semi-structured interviews

*LaTeX label: `tab:qualitative_codebook`*

| Theme | Subtheme | Supporting Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| **Technological Empowerment** | Lowering Creative Barriers | “The system allowed me to create traditional patterns without having to learn complicated production techniques.” (P03)<br>“I could explore different visual ideas even though I had little previous experience with this type of folk art.” (P09) |
| — | Cultural Knowledge Accessibility | “The descriptions helped me understand why particular patterns and symbols were used.” (P06)<br>“I learned about the cultural meanings of some elements while preparing the prompts.” (P12) |
| — | Supporting Cultural Expression | “The framework gave me new possibilities for combining traditional motifs with contemporary design styles.” (P04)<br>“It helped me imagine how traditional patterns could be applied to modern products.” (P15) |
| **Challenges of AI Integration** | Cultural Homogenization | “Some generated images looked similar to designs I had seen before, even when different cultural elements were used.” (P02)<br>“The modern visual styles sometimes became more noticeable than the traditional features.” (P11) |
| — | Loss of Cultural Context | “A pattern may look attractive, but its original meaning is not always clear in the generated design.” (P07)<br>“The generated image sometimes preserved the shape of a symbol while changing its cultural interpretation.” (P14) |
| — | Limitations of Automated Evaluation | “The evaluation could identify visual problems, but it could not always explain whether the cultural meaning was appropriate.” (P05)<br>“A high score did not necessarily mean that the generated design represented the traditional culture accurately.” (P16) |
| **Human–AI Collaboration** | Human Agency | “I preferred to decide which cultural elements should remain in the final design rather than accepting the generated result directly.” (P01)<br>“The system provided alternatives, but I still needed to make the final creative decisions.” (P10) |
| — | Iterative Creative Refinement | “I adjusted the prompts several times before the result matched what I wanted to express.” (P08)<br>“The feedback helped me identify which parts of the generated image needed further improvement.” (P13) |
| — | Cultural Expertise and Authenticity | “Someone familiar with traditional craftsmanship should still check whether the cultural details are correct.” (P17)<br>“AI can help generate ideas, but understanding the cultural background is still necessary.” (P06) |

